{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BLOAT-REMOVAL MATRIX, part 2 of 2 — every remaining unified-zero diff hunk H33-H61 is a separate row. B=da355b1c7ed7d34fe504cfddfde2e11ec7a3d823; C=601de2a0b31a5453ee82905e696c1949dda619be. V=scripts/jira-pressure-test/e2e_validation_probe.sh. “C:∅ near N” denotes intentional removal at that exact candidate location.\n\n| Hunk | Verdict | Before -> after citation | Bloat-removal judgment |\n| H33 | PASS | V B:254-257 -> C:254 | Removed verbose log-format/GNU-PCRE history; retained exact field-M meaning and BSD-portable awk choice. |\n| H34 | PASS | V B:271 -> C:∅ near 267 | Removed “Step 1” narration; create command and Phase 1 heading already state the action. |\n| H35 | PASS | V B:276 -> C:272 | Replaced output-shape narration with the concise current reason for ID extraction. |\n| H36 | PASS | V B:287 -> C:∅ near 282 | Removed “Step 2”; the adjacent echo and run_filtered_reconciler call self-describe the pass. |\n| H37 | PASS | V B:292 -> C:∅ near 286 | Removed “Step 3”; binding_state/check and assertion immediately below are explicit. |\n| H38 | PASS | V B:306 -> C:∅ near 299 | Removed “Step 3a”; jira_summary assertion names the behavior. |\n| H39 | PASS | V B:314 -> C:∅ near 306 | Removed “Step 3b”; jira_priority assertion names High. |\n| H40 | PASS | V B:322 -> C:∅ near 313 | Removed “Step 3c”; jira_type assertion names Task. |\n| H41 | PASS | V B:330 -> C:∅ near 320 | Removed “Step 3d”; label reads/assertions name both required labels. |\n| H42 | PASS | V B:343 -> C:∅ near 332 | Removed “Step 3e”; rebar-id assertion is self-explanatory. |\n| H43 | PASS | V B:358-360 -> C:347 | Removed stale “CLI has no edit” history and step numbering; retained the event-sourced/no-ticket-file reason for CLI edits. |\n| H44 | PASS | V B:367 -> C:∅ near 353 | Removed “Step 5”; edit --priority and assertion self-describe the operation. |\n| H45 | PASS | V B:374 -> C:∅ near 359 | Removed “Step 6”; ticket comment command self-describes. |\n| H46 | PASS | V B:378 -> C:∅ near 362 | Removed “Step 7”; ticket tag command self-describes. |\n| H47 | PASS | V B:382 -> C:∅ near 365 | Removed “Step 8”; adjacent reconciler message/call self-describe. |\n| H48 | PASS | V B:387-389 -> C:∅ near 369 | Removed Step 9/9a narration; jira_summary assertion directly states expected update. |\n| H49 | PASS | V B:397 -> C:∅ near 376 | Removed 9b narration; priority Low assertion is explicit. |\n| H50 | PASS | V B:405 -> C:∅ near 383 | Removed 9c narration; Jira comment lookup/assertion is explicit. |\n| H51 | PASS | V B:413 -> C:∅ near 390 | Removed 9d narration; Jira label lookup/assertion is explicit. |\n| H52 | PASS | V B:429-430 -> C:406 | Removed step numbering; retained the adapter-wrapper policy that code alone does not explain. |\n| H53 | PASS | V B:442 -> C:∅ near 417 | Removed Step 11; AcliClient.add_comment call is explicit. |\n| H54 | PASS | V B:459 -> C:434 | Replaced vague “wait briefly” with the current reason: Jira index settling. |\n| H55 | PASS | V B:462 -> C:∅ near 436 | Removed Step 12; adjacent inbound-sync message/call is explicit. |\n| H56 | PASS | V B:467 -> C:∅ near 440 | Removed Step 13; local_title lookup/assertion is explicit. |\n| H57 | PASS | V B:472-474 -> C:445 | Removed tentative implementation narration; retained the live local-wins tolerance explaining the alternate accepted title. |\n| H58 | PASS | V B:490-492 -> C:461 | Removed empirical pass-count history; retained bounded eventual convergence as the pre-idempotency reason. |\n| H59 | PASS | V B:501 -> C:∅ near 469 | Removed narration duplicated by the named three-pass loop and exact zero checks. |\n| H60 | PASS | V B:544 -> C:∅ near 511 | Removed Step 18; Phase 66 heading and Jira delete call self-describe cleanup. |\n| H61 | PASS | V B:562 -> C:∅ near 528 | Removed Step 19; local delete command and pass/fail names self-describe cleanup. |\n\nBloat-removal result: PASS, 61/61 hunks. No historical incident/bug narrative or obvious mechanical step narration remains in an edited block. Every retained replacement explains a current safety, recovery, portability, conflict-policy, or manual-operation constraint that executable code alone would not communicate.\n\nVerifier-syntax note: the ticket-stored shell guard is BRE-styled but git diff’s ignore-matching-lines matcher is ERE. Independently reproduced against C: the escaped-grouping pattern returned rc=1 with 28,961 diff bytes, while the semantically identical proper ERE returned rc=0 with zero diff bytes. Certification therefore relies on the proper ERE result plus the explicit changed-line audit (227/227 comment-or-blank), without altering signed ticket material.\n\nNo full test suite was run. The exact SHA was confirmed before and after review, and no tracked or untracked candidate file was edited by this reviewer."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789000424835721001,"uuid":"b4d085ee-c9cd-4494-b918-4b48b55fb1e2"}